<title>USA: Carolina 767 MW nuke unit boosting power.</title>
<headline>Carolina 767 MW nuke unit boosting power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carolina Power &amp; Light Co's 767 Brunswick nuclear power unit 1 was boosting electricity output Thursday, returning to the grid from scheduled maintenance and refueling, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>The Southport, N.C. unit was operating at 15 percent of capacity and &quot;increasing power,&quot; the NRC said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>Brunswick 1 was shut down Oct 5 for the refueling.</p>
<p>The 754 MW Brunswick unit 2 was operating at 100 percent of capacity as of early Thursday, the NRC said.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
